00:09:43.848 --> 00:09:47.199
- The only way to get
somebody to over-deliver

00:09:47.199 --> 00:09:51.621
is to attack their own
selfishness, their's.

00:09:51.621 --> 00:09:53.289
You're selfish 'cause you want more

00:09:53.289 --> 00:09:55.346
out of your team to help you.

00:09:55.346 --> 00:09:57.167
Well, the best way to get that to happen

00:09:57.167 --> 00:09:59.928
is to over-deliver
against their selfishness.

00:09:59.928 --> 00:10:02.434
I do believe that guilt is a huge driver

00:10:02.434 --> 00:10:04.543
because, and there's something that I,

00:10:04.543 --> 00:10:05.635
I believe in human beings.

00:10:05.635 --> 00:10:07.553
I mean, some people don't
have self-awareness,

00:10:07.553 --> 00:10:09.802
or empathy, or these emotional feelings.

00:10:09.802 --> 00:10:12.169
So many people, like, it's amazing to me

00:10:12.169 --> 00:10:14.151
now living 20 years professionally, like,

00:10:14.151 --> 00:10:16.712
how many people are not
confused eventually.

00:10:16.712 --> 00:10:18.654
They may be emotional at
the time you fire them,

00:10:18.654 --> 00:10:21.841
or not reward them, but
boy, every time I run

00:10:21.841 --> 00:10:24.742
into somebody four, seven,
nine years down the line;

00:10:24.742 --> 00:10:27.228
I've had a very good
track-record of them saying,

00:10:27.228 --> 00:10:28.896
"Yeah, I know why you did that."

00:10:28.896 --> 00:10:29.992
I mean, like crazy stuff like,

00:10:29.992 --> 00:10:31.610
"I had a drug problem!"

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:32.967
There was, like, you know, stuff!

